<title>USA: Gibson to launch &quot;Batman&quot; product line.</title>
<headline>Gibson to launch &quot;Batman&quot; product line.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gibson Greetings Inc said on Friday that it would introduce a new line of pop-up greeting cards, dress-up magnets and paper action assembly kits centered around the upcoming &quot;Batman &amp; Robin&quot; motion picture.</p>
<p>Gibson, a greeting card and party goods company, said it has the rights to Batman &amp; Robin through a licensing agreement with Warner Bros Consumer Products and Warner Bros subsidiary DC Comics. Warner Bros Consumer Products is a unit of Time Warner Inc.</p>
<p>Gibson also said it is preparing a product line for the film's video release in time for Christmas.</p>
<p>((New York Newsdesk 212 859 1610))</p>
